[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent complex LU component admission and output integrity

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LU-COMPLEX-RHS-FINITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reject either nonfinite complex RHS component independently
STATEMENT: >>>
Dense LU complex solves shall reject an incorrectly sized RHS or a nonfinite
real or imaginary RHS component as InvalidInput, even when the other component
is finite. Invalid data shall not be admitted and relabeled as a later generic
numerical failure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: complex_lu_finiteness each_rhs_component_must_be_finite_independently.
Well-conditioned unit matrices isolate RHS validation; NaN and both infinities
are independently placed in each component, including the paired case.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LU-COMPLEX-OUTPUT-FINITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Refuse a solution with either unrepresentable component
STATEMENT: >>>
Dense LU shall return NumericalFailure rather than success when a complex
solution has a nonfinite real or imaginary component, even if the other
component is representable. Valid well-conditioned finite known solutions
shall preserve both complex components.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: overflow_in_either_solution_component_cannot_be_returned_as_success
uses scalar A=0.5 with finite RHS(MAX,1) and(1,MAX), including negative signs.
complex_known_solutions_preserve_both_components forms RHS from exact small
integer/quarter products and independent known solutions;96 Proptest cases,
seed2026111910. No production residual routine supplies expected answers.
Implementation: src/backend.rs DenseLu::solve_complex_rhs, unchanged here.
<<<
